{# One accordion panel, everywhere in the wiki.

   `<details>`/`<summary>`, not a button plus a JS-toggled div. The browser already has a
   disclosure widget: it is keyboard operable, it announces its state to a screen reader, the
   browser's own find-in-page opens it to reveal a match, and it needs no JavaScript at all --
   which is what ADR-0005's "vanilla JS and htmx only" is asking for. The markup it replaces
   needed `data-toggle="collapse"`, matching ids on two elements, `aria-expanded`,
   `aria-controls`, `role="region"` and a listener in yw-core.js to keep them in step.

   Four surfaces used to spell that out separately -- the bazar entry list, the syndication
   list, the pages accordion and the {{panel}} action -- with the ids built differently in
   each. They share this now, so an accordion looks and behaves the same wherever it appears.

   Parameters:
     summary   markup for the closed state (raw)
     body      markup revealed when open (raw)
     open      start open (the first panel of an {{accordion}}, say)
     class     extra classes on the <details>
     attrs     raw attribute string, for callers that carry data attributes (entry html_data) #}
<details class="yw-accordion__item {{ class|default('') }}"{{ open|default(false) ? ' open' : '' }} {{ attrs|default('')|raw }}>
    <summary class="yw-accordion__summary">{{ summary|raw }}</summary>
    <div class="yw-accordion__body">{{ body|raw }}</div>
</details>
